course: dictionary
lesson: 9397
title: Sprinter: a runner for short races
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sprinter is a runner who races over short distances very fast. Look at the clues around the word: «Usain Bolt ran 100 m in 9.58 seconds in 2009.» A short distance and a time in seconds tell you a sprinter's race is quick.
explain: The word also works for animals. Any animal or person who can run very fast for a short time can be called a sprinter. «The cheetah is the sprinter, the fastest runner on land.» The words fastest and on land are the clues.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. "The cheetah is the very fast runner, the fastest runner on land" still makes sense, so you have the right idea. Context and a quick swap work together.
fact: A sprinter is a runner who races over short distances very fast.
fact: «Usain Bolt ran 100 m in 9.58 seconds in 2009», and that time was still the world record.
fact: Sprinters reach top speed around halfway, and the winner is often the one who slows least.
fact: The cheetah is the fastest runner on land, so it is the sprinter of the animal world.
fact: «A brown bear can run about 50 kilometres an hour in short bursts», which is faster than the fastest human sprinter.
exercise: What is a sprinter? | A runner who races over very long distances | A swimmer who floats slowly | A walker in the park | *A runner who races over short distances very fast
exercise: Which animal is called the sprinter in «The cheetah is the sprinter, the fastest runner on land»? | The jaguar | *The cheetah | The wolf | The leopard
exercise: Sprinters' times are compared, and a lower time means what? | A longer race | A bigger crowd | A slower sprinter | *A faster sprinter
test: Which race is a sprinter's race? | A very long walk for hours | *The 100 m | A slow stroll around the park
test: «A brown bear can run about 50 kilometres an hour in short bursts.» What does in short bursts mean? | *For a short time | Without stopping | For a whole day | Only in the water
exam: Which of these is a sprinter? | A snail on a wall | A sleeping cat | A tortoise crossing a road | *A cheetah running to catch its meal
